# Keep the build context lean — only what `go build ./cmd/api` actually needs.
# Anything excluded here is invisible to the builder stage, which means a
# faster `docker build` and no risk of secrets / large binaries leaking in.

# VCS + editor noise
.git
.github
.vscode
.idea
*.swp

# Local secrets and config — never bake into an image.
.env
.env.*
!env.sample

# Local build outputs (the host's `make build` / `go build ./cmd/api` etc.).
# Anchored with a leading `/` so they only match at the build-context root —
# unanchored names would also match `./cmd/api/`, `./internal/main/...`, etc.
# That's exactly the bug that broke our docker build once: bare `api` excluded
# the cmd/api source directory and the build couldn't find main.go.
bin/
/main
/api
/url-shortener
*.exe
*.test
*.out
coverage*

# Docs that aren't compiled in. The `docs/` Go package IS imported (Swagger),
# so don't exclude that. Markdown is fine to drop.
*.md

# Toolchain / CI configs not needed inside the image.
.golangci.yml
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
docker-compose*.yml

# Migrations live next to the API in source, but inside the image we don't
# ship them — the `migrate` compose service mounts them from the host.
migrations/

# Misc
scripts/
